{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And the Mishkan you shall make of ten curtains.</b> To serve as its roof and as partitions outside the planks — for the curtains were suspended behind them to cover them." "<b>Fine twisted linen, and tekhelet, and purple, and crimson.</b> Here are four kinds combined in one thread: one of linen and three of wool. And each and every thread is sixfold — so here are four kinds as they are twisted together: twenty-four strands to the thread (Yoma 71b)." "<b>Cherubim, the work of a weaver.</b> Cherubim were figured in them through their weaving — not through embroidery, which is work with a needle, but through weaving on two sides: one face on this side and one face on the other — a lion on this side and an eagle on that side — as one weaves silk sashes that are called in la'az פיישי״שא."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {2 "the la'az is Old French pelisses (or a related dialectal form), referring to ornamental woven silk articles."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:37.369262296Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}